== Notes ==

*Requires [[Hordes of the Underdark]].
* The "ability to cast level 9 spells" may be better understood as the ability to learn level 9 spells (as [[wizard]]s are not required to know spells of the highest level they can cast).
* This feat provides the benefits of [[quicken spell]] without the need to use a [[spell slot]] of a higher level than normal. In particular, casting a quickened spell while [[haste]]ned does not further reduce casting time, as both quickened and hastened have the same effect on casting time.
*The in-game description is incorrect in regards to interruption and countering.
**Quickened spells can be interrupted if damage is received and the [[concentration]] check is failed. However, a quickened spell does not provoke an [[attack of opportunity]], so the chance of receiving damage at the right moment is decreased.
**Quickened spells can be countered normally, unless the caster is hastened. If the caster is hastened, the counterspeller must also be hastened to successfully counterspell.
*This feat can be selected by [[bard]]s. However, a bard cannot achieve the 9th level spell requirement on its own, so 17 levels of [[cleric]], [[druid]], or [[wizard]], or 18 levels of [[sorcerer]], would be needed.
* Auto quicken spell does not add a metamagic icon to the spells it affects. The only indication that this feat is having an effect is the reduced casting time.

==Custom content notes==

*A custom class must have this feat in their feat list, or that class will not be able to select it as a general feat.
